# BUG (engines disagree): under `kanso play`, a file's own function `step`
# is replaced by std/list's record `list/step` on the native engine when the
# file imports std/list. The interpreter calls the function.
#
#   kanso play step.kso --interp   prints 4
#   kanso play step.kso            prints list/step 3
#
# The same function inside a module directory, run with `kanso run`, `build`
# or `--interp`, prints 4 everywhere. Expected: 4 on every engine (the
# 2026-10-12 gavel "arms travel with the value, and a file names only what
# it can see" says a file's own name wins).
import "std/list"

fn step x
  x + 1

print "{step 3} {list/sum [1 2]}"
